      "worked_solution": "To make our estimation, we proceed as follows:\n\n- We start at $y=56$ on the vertical axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/a9d57651c5c342c3d619a20cfae2bc632df47f8924d49f400ed764870b7ae900.png)\n\n- Then, we move right until we intersect the trend line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/c816d47fc84f31c3a436818777d9473b68e9d8468051c40fe9b7b94005cc89ee.png)\n\n- Finally, we move down until we intersect the horizontal axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944892/assets/e6cbfe34a6e3bd002171d2474542a12c66b7d88ce5989b0fbb4b3542f76a2155.png)\n\nTherefore, the population was $56\\,000$ in approximately the year $2000+10=2010.$",
